{
  "id": "beer-distribution-game-cla",
  "name": "Beer Distribution Game",
  "description": "The classic 'Beer Game' supply chain simulation developed at MIT Sloan. Demonstrates the bullwhip effect where small changes in retail demand cause increasingly larger fluctuations at each upstream stage (retailer, wholesaler, distributor, factory). Reference: Based on System Dynamics supply chain models (Sterman, 2000). Source: https://systemdynamics.org/",
